(192860, 10788, 3018, '<td valign="top">Very nice colors.  I wish it wasn''t so dark, but it is still great.  Maybe you can crop a little more from the top.  Good luck!</td>', 'Very nice colors.  I wish it wasn''t so dark, but it is still great.  Maybe you can crop a little more from the top.  Good luck!', '2003-01-16 17:52:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(192861, 10962, 5100, '<td valign="top">I love the way the water looks, great!</td>', 'I love the way the water looks, great!', '2003-01-16 17:52:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(192862, 10939, 811, '<td valign="top">Just my opinion, but I think the path needs to be more "in" the picture.  Maybe a little further to the left, then it would have a clearer entry.  It is  a good method of drawing the eyes up and into the picture.  Very well taken.  Your snow is white and not bluish or blownout!</td>', 'Just my opinion, but I think the path needs to be more "in" the picture.  Maybe a little further to the left, then it would have a clearer entry.  It is  a good method of drawing the eyes up and into the picture.  Very well taken.  Your snow is white and not bluish or blownout!', '2003-01-16 17:54:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(192864, 10795, 5100, '<td valign="top">This is weird I don''t like it :/</td>', 'This is weird I don''t like it :/', '2003-01-16 17:55:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(192865, 10901, 527, '<td valign="top">This is one of those images that I have a difficult time suggesting what it might need as far as composition goes because I have no idea what the rest of the scene looks like. I feel that it needs something more in the way of composition because I feel that the ice is too centered. The ice is beautiful and dramatic but the composition doesn''t really support that. Maybe a vertical shot with the dark rock on the right side and the white of the ice hugging the left edge and eliminating some of the dark areas on the left side.  6  -Tim</td>', 'This is one of those images that I have a difficult time suggesting what it might need as far as composition goes because I have no idea what the rest of the scene looks like. I feel that it needs something more in the way of composition because I feel that the ice is too centered. The ice is beautiful and dramatic but the composition doesn''t really support that. Maybe a vertical shot with the dark rock on the right side and the white of the ice hugging the left edge and eliminating some of the dark areas on the left side.  6  -Tim', '2003-01-16 17:57:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(192868, 10930, 811, '<td valign="top">I realize it is the curve of the lake, but hte left side being lower than the right makes it feel lopsided, even though the picture is probably even.  Maybe include more of the shore on the left, or crop it before it  further on the right so that the section that feels curved would be eliminated.  Bet this is gorgeous in summer!</td>', 'I realize it is the curve of the lake, but hte left side being lower than the right makes it feel lopsided, even though the picture is probably even.  Maybe include more of the shore on the left, or crop it before it  further on the right so that the section that feels curved would be eliminated.  Bet this is gorgeous in summer!', '2003-01-16 18:01:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(192869, 10818, 527, '<td valign="top">Now this has some dramatic lines. I realy like the composition here as well as the texture and detail. I feel that it is slightly overexposed though as evidenced by the overly bright water and the slightly washed out area in the foreground. 8  -Tim</td>', 'Now this has some dramatic lines. I realy like the composition here as well as the texture and detail. I feel that it is slightly overexposed though as evidenced by the overly bright water and the slightly washed out area in the foreground. 8  -Tim', '2003-01-16 18:01:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(192871, 10875, 811, '<td valign="top">It seems pixelated in the weeds in front (over sharpened, maybe?) and there is noise in the sky.   NeatImage (you can get a free download) is dpc legal and awesome at removing noise.</td>', 'It seems pixelated in the weeds in front (over sharpened, maybe?) and there is noise in the sky.   NeatImage (you can get a free download) is dpc legal and awesome at removing noise.', '2003-01-16 18:02:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(192872, 10737, 811, '<td valign="top">Awesome detail.  The only suggestion I would make is to consider the composition so that the "lit" part of the moon is in the bottom of the frame, then it would have the negative space to really emphasize the subject.</td>', 'Awesome detail.  The only suggestion I would make is to consider the composition so that the "lit" part of the moon is in the bottom of the frame, then it would have the negative space to really emphasize the subject.', '2003-01-16 18:05:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(192873, 10779, 811, '<td valign="top">The fences do a nice job of forming "converging lines.  I think if there junction was more readily viewable, it would be even more effective.</td>', 'The fences do a nice job of forming "converging lines.  I think if there junction was more readily viewable, it would be even more effective.', '2003-01-16 18:07:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(192874, 10736, 527, '<td valign="top">This would be fun to take at different times of the day and year to see the different affects of the sky and lighting. I really like how you have this cropped by showing only a necessary amount of the foreground foliage and lots of sky. It really gives me a good feeling. A polarizer filter or a split neutral density filter probably would have helped to darken and enhance the sky a little more. Nice job.  8  -Tim</td>', 'This would be fun to take at different times of the day and year to see the different affects of the sky and lighting. I really like how you have this cropped by showing only a necessary amount of the foreground foliage and lots of sky. It really gives me a good feeling. A polarizer filter or a split neutral density filter probably would have helped to darken and enhance the sky a little more. Nice job.  8  -Tim', '2003-01-16 18:07:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(192876, 10892, 3575, '<td valign="top">Hey, works for me! Great macro. and DOF</td>', 'Hey, works for me! Great macro. and DOF', '2003-01-16 18:09:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(192877, 10885, 3575, '<td valign="top">Looks lika a tropical island. Nice -- I think I would like it in color too.</td>', 'Looks lika a tropical island. Nice -- I think I would like it in color too.', '2003-01-16 18:10:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(192878, 10919, 527, '<td valign="top">This is a little too simplistic for me and I don''t like the bits of branches stick out on the left top. Maybe if the sky was more dramatic looking it would work better for me. It''s a good idea but it needs some more work.  5  -Tim</td>', 'This is a little too simplistic for me and I don''t like the bits of branches stick out on the left top. Maybe if the sky was more dramatic looking it would work better for me. It''s a good idea but it needs some more work.  5  -Tim', '2003-01-16 18:10:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(192879, 10990, 811, '<td valign="top">Oddly enough, I like what I consider negative space at the top of the picture.  It makes the landscape look isolated and barren.  Good use of bw, I think.</td>', 'Oddly enough, I like what I consider negative space at the top of the picture.  It makes the landscape look isolated and barren.  Good use of bw, I think.', '2003-01-16 18:10:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(192882, 10746, 811, '<td valign="top">It seems that you were trying to capture the mist/clouds coming in over the ridge, but the water is so awesome, I wish you had gotten more of that, and less of the top stuff.  Makes me want to go there.</td>', 'It seems that you were trying to capture the mist/clouds coming in over the ridge, but the water is so awesome, I wish you had gotten more of that, and less of the top stuff.  Makes me want to go there.', '2003-01-16 18:17:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(192883, 11019, 527, '<td valign="top">As much as I like this photo I am having a difficult time viewing it as a landscape because the focus is so squarely upon the ice formation rather than the landscape or an area of the environment. It''s too specific. If you would have stepped back and photographed this formation in it''s environment I think it would have fit the them better. It is cropped very well, has nice colors and is technically well done. 6  -Tim</td>', 'As much as I like this photo I am having a difficult time viewing it as a landscape because the focus is so squarely upon the ice formation rather than the landscape or an area of the environment. It''s too specific. If you would have stepped back and photographed this formation in it''s environment I think it would have fit the them better. It is cropped very well, has nice colors and is technically well done. 6  -Tim', '2003-01-16 18:20:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(192884, 10995, 573, '<td valign="top">I like how the curve of the beach leads the eye to the building.  the sunset colors are great and the neat and far detail is what landscape photos are all about.  One of my top ten.</td>', 'I like how the curve of the beach leads the eye to the building.  the sunset colors are great and the neat and far detail is what landscape photos are all about.  One of my top ten.', '2003-01-16 18:23:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(192886, 10737, 5100, '<td valign="top">This is one of the most well done moon shots I have ever seen...<br/>great picture!</td>', 'This is one of the most well done moon shots I have ever seen...great picture!', '2003-01-16 18:27:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(192887, 10753, 527, '<td valign="top">I hate to say this but I really don''t like the sepia color on this photo. It just doesn''t work for me. It feels old instead of fresh. I think a straight black and white would have been much better and would have kept the timelessness of the scene. The composition is a little off. I would have framed the scene more to the left and down a bit to show the entire boat in the lower left corner. The mast that is sick up from the bottom edge is very distracting as well. This is a very beautiful location but I don''t feel that you captured it as well as it could have been. 5  -Tim</td>', 'I hate to say this but I really don''t like the sepia color on this photo. It just doesn''t work for me. It feels old instead of fresh. I think a straight black and white would have been much better and would have kept the timelessness of the scene. The composition is a little off. I would have framed the scene more to the left and down a bit to show the entire boat in the lower left corner. The mast that is sick up from the bottom edge is very distracting as well. This is a very beautiful location but I don''t feel that you captured it as well as it could have been. 5  -Tim', '2003-01-16 18:27:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(192888, 11010, 1647, '<td valign="top">Good photo - the colours are rich and the focus is nice.  I''m curious as to why you chose portrait instead of landscape though.  There is a bit too much sky for my taste and landscape orientation may have pushed the horizon up to about 1/3 from the top.  Otherwise though the photo is nice - the foreground is particularly interesting</td>', 'Good photo - the colours are rich and the focus is nice.  I''m curious as to why you chose portrait instead of landscape though.  There is a bit too much sky for my taste and landscape orientation may have pushed the horizon up to about 1/3 from the top.  Otherwise though the photo is nice - the foreground is particularly interesting', '2003-01-16 18:28:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(192890, 10784, 5100, '<td valign="top">dramatic shot, very well executed.</td>', 'dramatic shot, very well executed.', '2003-01-16 18:33:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(192892, 10849, 573, '<td valign="top">I love these deep orange sunsets.  I only wish there was more detail in the distance and less forground because for me the picture is in the clouds.</td>', 'I love these deep orange sunsets.  I only wish there was more detail in the distance and less forground because for me the picture is in the clouds.', '2003-01-16 18:35:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(192896, 10788, 573, '<td valign="top">The sureal color is way cool.  Good detail in the forground and great use of negative space.  one of my top ten this week.</td>', 'The sureal color is way cool.  Good detail in the forground and great use of negative space.  one of my top ten this week.', '2003-01-16 18:39:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(192898, 10925, 573, '<td valign="top">My first impression was that this was a very grainy image, then on closer look I see just a lot of wonderful texture.  Why did you choose monochrime, I wonder how this looked in color?</td>', 'My first impression was that this was a very grainy image, then on closer look I see just a lot of wonderful texture.  Why did you choose monochrime, I wonder how this looked in color?', '2003-01-16 18:47:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(192900, 10980, 573, '<td valign="top">I like the misterious Hound of the Baskervills feel of this image, I would like to see some reference point I could use to get a feel of size and distance.</td>', 'I like the misterious Hound of the Baskervills feel of this image, I would like to see some reference point I could use to get a feel of size and distance.', '2003-01-16 18:53:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(192901, 10840, 1570, '<td valign="top">i like this picture, but it would be better if the horses weren''t leaving...</td>', 'i like this picture, but it would be better if the horses weren''t leaving...', '2003-01-16 19:06:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(192905, 10951, 3447, '<td valign="top">I like this photograph a lot.  Some nits - crop a bit less on right side and a bit more at bottom to eliminate wires.</td>', 'I like this photograph a lot.  Some nits - crop a bit less on right side and a bit more at bottom to eliminate wires.', '2003-01-16 19:17:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(192906, 11044, 1863, '<td valign="top">Lovely Landscape. I like the look of fog over the river. Keep up the good work! -Annida</td>', 'Lovely Landscape. I like the look of fog over the river. Keep up the good work! -Annida', '2003-01-16 19:19:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(192907, 10840, 1863, '<td valign="top">I love the shape of the trees here.  The colour of the grass and sky is superb. Too bad the riders aren''t moving into the photo instead of out. Lovely work regardless, I give you a 9 :) -Annida</td>', 'I love the shape of the trees here.  The colour of the grass and sky is superb. Too bad the riders aren''t moving into the photo instead of out. Lovely work regardless, I give you a 9 :) -Annida', '2003-01-16 19:21:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(192908, 10910, 1863, '<td valign="top">A very beautiful landscape to see out of your window *gets jealous*...  I wish I could see more of it. 9!! -Annida</td>', 'A very beautiful landscape to see out of your window *gets jealous*...  I wish I could see more of it. 9!! -Annida', '2003-01-16 19:22:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(192909, 11006, 1863, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful.. my only problem is that it lacks vibrancy. I''m not sure if that''s an issue or not.. or maybe the picture needs to be bigger to show how grandeur this place is... keep up the good work though, I give you a 9!! -Annida</td>', 'This is beautiful.. my only problem is that it lacks vibrancy. I''m not sure if that''s an issue or not.. or maybe the picture needs to be bigger to show how grandeur this place is... keep up the good work though, I give you a 9!! -Annida', '2003-01-16 19:23:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(192911, 10990, 1863, '<td valign="top">This is one of the strange photos that I think are so beautiful for being black and white, can you tell I love black and white? I love the sky, and how barren the ground looks. I give you a 10! -Annida</td>', 'This is one of the strange photos that I think are so beautiful for being black and white, can you tell I love black and white? I love the sky, and how barren the ground looks. I give you a 10! -Annida', '2003-01-16 19:24:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(192917, 10847, 4815, '<td valign="top">A nice study in almost B&amp;W. I like the single left tree balancing the tree line on the left. And just the right amount of sky to set the mood. The snow bits on the trunks and icing on the branches are much needed to break up the stark dark vertical and horizontal lines. Although it may not have been possible from your vantage point, I would like the man made structure to be absent ( a minor point ).  Otherwise a very pleasing image.</td>', 'A nice study in almost B&W. I like the single left tree balancing the tree line on the left. And just the right amount of sky to set the mood. The snow bits on the trunks and icing on the branches are much needed to break up the stark dark vertical and horizontal lines. Although it may not have been possible from your vantage point, I would like the man made structure to be absent ( a minor point ).  Otherwise a very pleasing image.', '2003-01-16 19:30:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(192919, 10884, 4815, '<td valign="top">There are some visually attractive elements in this image. I especially like the graceful powerful sweep of the torrential river. Flowing lines contrast well to the logically solid jutting prescence of the rocks. It looks like a difficult photo situation with blazing boring sky and deep dark shadows. You can''t have detail in both. I personnally find the sky and trees too harsh ( just me ). If possible I would omit those two elements altogether and just concentrate on composing an image demonstrating the river power. Or if you are lucky enough to happen to be there on a day with a more interesting cloud pattern. These are thoughts only. It''s your photo, and if you''re happy with it that''s all that matters. Keep up the good work.</td>', 'There are some visually attractive elements in this image. I especially like the graceful powerful sweep of the torrential river. Flowing lines contrast well to the logically solid jutting prescence of the rocks. It looks like a difficult photo situation with blazing boring sky and deep dark shadows. You can''t have detail in both. I personnally find the sky and trees too harsh ( just me ). If possible I would omit those two elements altogether and just concentrate on composing an image demonstrating the river power. Or if you are lucky enough to happen to be there on a day with a more interesting cloud pattern. These are thoughts only. It''s your photo, and if you''re happy with it that''s all that matters. Keep up the good work.', '2003-01-16 19:39:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(192920, 10903, 4411, '<td valign="top">Wow, made me want to find out where this place is. Hawaii eh? I just ended up spending half an hour looking through a couple of galleries of the area on pbase : )<br/> <br/>The first thing that grabs my eye is the mist, then the grass framing the image perfectly, then the layers in between. This is great. 10<br/></td>', 'Wow, made me want to find out where this place is. Hawaii eh? I just ended up spending half an hour looking through a couple of galleries of the area on pbase : ) The first thing that grabs my eye is the mist, then the grass framing the image perfectly, then the layers in between. This is great. 10', '2003-01-16 19:41:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(192922, 10999, 4815, '<td valign="top">This is a good solid composition. I especially like the glistening road and hint of tire tracks. The beautiful tree silhouette breaks up the monotonous shy perfectly. I also like how you captured the dual tree backgrounds before the mist disappeared. The color of green in the image brings a vibrant touch of life. This is a good image that would go well in a photo essay series. Good work.</td>', 'This is a good solid composition. I especially like the glistening road and hint of tire tracks. The beautiful tree silhouette breaks up the monotonous shy perfectly. I also like how you captured the dual tree backgrounds before the mist disappeared. The color of green in the image brings a vibrant touch of life. This is a good image that would go well in a photo essay series. Good work.', '2003-01-16 19:44:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(192923, 10799, 2158, '<td valign="top">Nice photo, but I''d have liked to see it a bit bigger, also a darker border (the colour of the house perhaps) would have worked better.</td>', 'Nice photo, but I''d have liked to see it a bit bigger, also a darker border (the colour of the house perhaps) would have worked better.', '2003-01-16 19:47:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(192924, 10704, 4815, '<td valign="top">A good local image that captures the classic historical serenity of the location. I like the bridge arching over the boat strerns. Those strerns are a nice color punch to the otherwise restrained color theme. The overhanging tree and meadow bit are lovely compositional accents. I also really like the kiss of light on the background stream. Beautiful touch. The overcast day really brings out those subtle colors. A worthy image.</td>', 'A good local image that captures the classic historical serenity of the location. I like the bridge arching over the boat strerns. Those strerns are a nice color punch to the otherwise restrained color theme. The overhanging tree and meadow bit are lovely compositional accents. I also really like the kiss of light on the background stream. Beautiful touch. The overcast day really brings out those subtle colors. A worthy image.', '2003-01-16 19:50:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(192927, 11036, 3447, '<td valign="top">Sure looks like Bay Area.  I heard about heavy rains recently in that area.  Would like to know location of this photograph.   JEM</td>', 'Sure looks like Bay Area.  I heard about heavy rains recently in that area.  Would like to know location of this photograph.   JEM', '2003-01-16 19:52:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(192931, 10895, 2158, '<td valign="top">I like your use of an unusual shape for this.  Not too sure about that white border though.</td>', 'I like your use of an unusual shape for this.  Not too sure about that white border though.', '2003-01-16 19:58:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(192932, 10983, 1647, '<td valign="top">I love the composition, and the reflection in the water.  The tower is a little washed out though.  It looks like the lighting was tough though (very bright sky, but very dark around pond).  I wonder if a polarising filter would have helped - others would know the answer to this.  Well done.</td>', 'I love the composition, and the reflection in the water.  The tower is a little washed out though.  It looks like the lighting was tough though (very bright sky, but very dark around pond).  I wonder if a polarising filter would have helped - others would know the answer to this.  Well done.', '2003-01-16 20:02:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(192934, 10948, 4815, '<td valign="top">Very spooky. Armageddon or what? The use of complimentary blue and yellow hues is interesting. An unusual but dramatic color choice for water. The steeple piercing the bottom centre  also has real kinetic thrust. This is an arresting diversion  from a theme that could be plauged by calendar attempts. Thank you for venturing so creatively. A good image.</td>', 'Very spooky. Armageddon or what? The use of complimentary blue and yellow hues is interesting. An unusual but dramatic color choice for water. The steeple piercing the bottom centre  also has real kinetic thrust. This is an arresting diversion  from a theme that could be plauged by calendar attempts. Thank you for venturing so creatively. A good image.', '2003-01-16 20:03:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(192935, 10746, 4615, '<td valign="top">This makes home sick!  Waaa.  the only thing I''d change is the intensity of reflection on the beach.  The detail and clarity of the mountain is awesome, and the mist on top just makes the picture.  9.  Good luck.</td>', 'This makes home sick!  Waaa.  the only thing I''d change is the intensity of reflection on the beach.  The detail and clarity of the mountain is awesome, and the mist on top just makes the picture.  9.  Good luck.', '2003-01-16 20:03:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(192936, 10711, 4815, '<td valign="top">There are some attractive elements in this image that are real attention grabbers. The really nice texture of the grain(?) strips. and those ultra vibrant green trees. Unfotunately modern lfe spoils the perfect pastoral scene with power lines. I personally would have cropped out the sky entirely and did a wide panaorama type image. Sky without detail tends to detract from the other lovely things you have recorded. If there was an interesting mist or puffy clouds that might add more to your image. Still a nice photo with fond memories I am sure. Good luck!</td>', 'There are some attractive elements in this image that are real attention grabbers. The really nice texture of the grain(?) strips. and those ultra vibrant green trees. Unfotunately modern lfe spoils the perfect pastoral scene with power lines. I personally would have cropped out the sky entirely and did a wide panaorama type image. Sky without detail tends to detract from the other lovely things you have recorded. If there was an interesting mist or puffy clouds that might add more to your image. Still a nice photo with fond memories I am sure. Good luck!', '2003-01-16 20:04:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(192937, 10838, 4615, '<td valign="top">Theres nothing to critique.  perfect 10.</td>', 'Theres nothing to critique.  perfect 10.', '2003-01-16 20:05:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(192938, 10818, 1647, '<td valign="top">It''s an interesting photo although the depth of field appears to be a bit shallow - the middle is in focus, but the grass at the bottom looks blurred and the bank at the top is blurred.  Without knowing the camera it''s difficult to say if there is much you could have done about this though.</td>', 'It''s an interesting photo although the depth of field appears to be a bit shallow - the middle is in focus, but the grass at the bottom looks blurred and the bank at the top is blurred.  Without knowing the camera it''s difficult to say if there is much you could have done about this though.', '2003-01-16 20:05:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(192939, 10970, 4615, '<td valign="top">great shot.</td>', 'great shot.', '2003-01-16 20:06:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(192941, 10909, 4615, '<td valign="top">Awesome.  wish i was there.</td>', 'Awesome.  wish i was there.', '2003-01-16 20:08:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(192942, 10891, 4615, '<td valign="top">very intense grass in the foreground.  I love the red roofs.</td>', 'very intense grass in the foreground.  I love the red roofs.', '2003-01-16 20:08:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(192944, 11011, 3447, '<td valign="top">THIRDS.  I believe this would have been a better photograph with more sky above the hawk.  Now, if that was not possible, perhaps more cropping at bottom.  Good capture of this large bird.</td>', 'THIRDS.  I believe this would have been a better photograph with more sky above the hawk.  Now, if that was not possible, perhaps more cropping at bottom.  Good capture of this large bird.', '2003-01-16 20:09:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(192945, 10893, 1647, '<td valign="top">That''s a lovely photo - definitely a printable image.  The colour is lovely, the water and clouds are a delight and the people provide a focus point.  Thankfully the grass-like plants aren''t in front of the people.  I have nothing bad to say except that the gress is just a fraction distracting.  I''m jealous.</td>', 'That''s a lovely photo - definitely a printable image.  The colour is lovely, the water and clouds are a delight and the people provide a focus point.  Thankfully the grass-like plants aren''t in front of the people.  I have nothing bad to say except that the gress is just a fraction distracting.  I''m jealous.', '2003-01-16 20:10:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(192946, 10822, 1647, '<td valign="top">It''s a shame that one tower is partly hidden.</td>', 'It''s a shame that one tower is partly hidden.', '2003-01-16 20:11:43.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(192947, 10904, 4615, '<td valign="top">All these NZ pics are making me too homesick.  Waaaa!  Akaroa is the most beautiful spot on earth.   great photo, will be one of my favorites.</td>', 'All these NZ pics are making me too homesick.  Waaaa!  Akaroa is the most beautiful spot on earth.   great photo, will be one of my favorites.', '2003-01-16 20:12:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(192948, 10716, 4615, '<td valign="top">Too many awesome pics this week.  This is one of them. 10</td>', 'Too many awesome pics this week.  This is one of them. 10', '2003-01-16 20:13:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(192949, 10702, 1647, '<td valign="top">Well, you''ve defintely gone for a simplistic shot - and done quite well.  It''s good to see that the sky behaved and was perfectly clear for you.  I love the contrast of the green and blue, and the trees add a lovely little focus point.  Is it possible to sharpen the trees a fraction?  Good work.</td>', 'Well, you''ve defintely gone for a simplistic shot - and done quite well.  It''s good to see that the sky behaved and was perfectly clear for you.  I love the contrast of the green and blue, and the trees add a lovely little focus point.  Is it possible to sharpen the trees a fraction?  Good work.', '2003-01-16 20:13:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(192950, 10963, 4615, '<td valign="top">Amazing subject.</td>', 'Amazing subject.', '2003-01-16 20:13:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(192951, 10990, 2752, '<td valign="top">I like the photo very much..grayscale works well and the starkness is very appealing..My only suggestion would be to change the title..I see a storm coming. It is one of my 10''s.</td>', 'I like the photo very much..grayscale works well and the starkness is very appealing..My only suggestion would be to change the title..I see a storm coming. It is one of my 10''s.', '2003-01-16 20:14:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(192952, 10830, 3447, '<td valign="top">And billions of people on this planet would give their souls to have such a home.</td>', 'And billions of people on this planet would give their souls to have such a home.', '2003-01-16 20:14:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(192953, 10831, 1647, '<td valign="top">I love the depth of field - it really separates the tree from the mountains.  Your framing and composition is lovely.  I have nothing bad to say except that it is perhaps a tiny bit blurry in the very foreground - perhaps wind or a long exposure?  Great photo though.</td>', 'I love the depth of field - it really separates the tree from the mountains.  Your framing and composition is lovely.  I have nothing bad to say except that it is perhaps a tiny bit blurry in the very foreground - perhaps wind or a long exposure?  Great photo though.', '2003-01-16 20:16:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(192955, 11041, 2752, '<td valign="top">the rock shots are great..I think your color choice does not do it justice...the background seems to float the farthest rock formations in air.</td>', 'the rock shots are great..I think your color choice does not do it justice...the background seems to float the farthest rock formations in air.', '2003-01-16 20:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(192956, 10778, 1647, '<td valign="top">An interesting variation on the landscape theme - and one that I like.  Nice composition (good focal point) and the depth of field helps this out.  Well done.</td>', 'An interesting variation on the landscape theme - and one that I like.  Nice composition (good focal point) and the depth of field helps this out.  Well done.', '2003-01-16 20:19:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(192957, 10892, 4615, '<td valign="top">Belongs in a macro challenge.  Would be a 7 or 8.</td>', 'Belongs in a macro challenge.  Would be a 7 or 8.', '2003-01-16 20:20:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(192958, 10918, 2752, '<td valign="top">I like the shadows and use of grayscale..well composed.</td>', 'I like the shadows and use of grayscale..well composed.', '2003-01-16 20:22:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(192959, 10957, 2752, '<td valign="top">lovely composition..good use of colors and good dof.  The tree on the right balances the photo nicely.</td>', 'lovely composition..good use of colors and good dof.  The tree on the right balances the photo nicely.', '2003-01-16 20:25:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(192961, 10867, 2752, '<td valign="top">Great shot..I think I see a storm coming?  The composition is very good and I like the lonely exspanse of it.</td>', 'Great shot..I think I see a storm coming?  The composition is very good and I like the lonely exspanse of it.', '2003-01-16 20:27:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(192962, 10772, 2158, '<td valign="top">I''d have cropped out some of the foreground because it is too dark to see much detail.</td>', 'I''d have cropped out some of the foreground because it is too dark to see much detail.', '2003-01-16 20:27:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(192964, 10958, 2752, '<td valign="top">well composed..love the patterns of snow on the beach and I can feel the wind.</td>', 'well composed..love the patterns of snow on the beach and I can feel the wind.', '2003-01-16 20:30:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(192966, 10925, 2752, '<td valign="top">very well composed shot...the undulating walk is in great contrast to the starkness of the trees and day. Well done in grayscale.</td>', 'very well composed shot...the undulating walk is in great contrast to the starkness of the trees and day. Well done in grayscale.', '2003-01-16 20:32:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(192974, 10856, 1135, '<td valign="top">Are you getting as many neg comments about lens flair as I am? (My shot this week is Morning Dew) I guess Im just a dummy but I think it adds to a shot like this, of course if we didn''t want it in the photo we would just shoot in another direction. Nice shot and good luck!</td>', 'Are you getting as many neg comments about lens flair as I am? (My shot this week is Morning Dew) I guess Im just a dummy but I think it adds to a shot like this, of course if we didn''t want it in the photo we would just shoot in another direction. Nice shot and good luck!', '2003-01-16 20:40:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(192975, 10885, 4338, '<td valign="top">seems a little dark or maybe would have looked better in color and not B&amp;W</td>', 'seems a little dark or maybe would have looked better in color and not B&W', '2003-01-16 20:40:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(192976, 10928, 1647, '<td valign="top">I like the photo but I don''t think the border suits it.  The blue is too bright, especially around the bottom.  Perhaps just straight black, or black with a white hairline inside it?</td>', 'I like the photo but I don''t think the border suits it.  The blue is too bright, especially around the bottom.  Perhaps just straight black, or black with a white hairline inside it?', '2003-01-16 20:40:44.000000', NULL, 1),
