(193791, 10975, 2700, '<td valign="top">perhaps if yo wer to get about 5inches lower and focus on the same subject, more feild would be in the picture and lessen the "harshness" of the barn''s white parts... I guess maybe a little less sky in post shot cropping... 10 however :) (some very poor photos this week :(</td>', 'perhaps if yo wer to get about 5inches lower and focus on the same subject, more feild would be in the picture and lessen the "harshness" of the barn''s white parts... I guess maybe a little less sky in post shot cropping... 10 however :) (some very poor photos this week :(', '2003-01-18 00:34:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(193792, 11026, 2700, '<td valign="top">EXCELLENT COLOR!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! (don''t really care for fake "frames" though) 9</td>', 'EXCELLENT COLOR!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! (don''t really care for fake "frames" though) 9', '2003-01-18 00:35:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(193793, 10746, 2700, '<td valign="top">I Think some photoshop "green" enhancment would make this photo amazing... 9</td>', 'I Think some photoshop "green" enhancment would make this photo amazing... 9', '2003-01-18 00:37:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(193794, 10808, 4811, '<td valign="top">This is a kind of abstract shot I always like. Simple, yet pleasing to look at. Who knows, it may be even better with no rocks, just two horizontal lines, and 3 different "textured" areas. The only technical problem is depth of field - its a little too narrow for this kind of picture. In this scenario I do believe the photo would be improved if everything was in focus.</td>', 'This is a kind of abstract shot I always like. Simple, yet pleasing to look at. Who knows, it may be even better with no rocks, just two horizontal lines, and 3 different "textured" areas. The only technical problem is depth of field - its a little too narrow for this kind of picture. In this scenario I do believe the photo would be improved if everything was in focus.', '2003-01-18 00:38:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(193795, 10838, 2700, '<td valign="top">I originally gave your pic a 7, after looking at it again... 10 :)</td>', 'I originally gave your pic a 7, after looking at it again... 10 :)', '2003-01-18 00:38:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(193796, 10917, 2700, '<td valign="top">The only problem I have with this picture is that there is no sense of depth... It looks too me like I am looking straight down; however,  if you were to move the camara and point it more towards the sky (still keeping all sand in the pic) - maybe only 6-10 degreess more, this would be very pleasing... oringaly a 6, after reevaluation 8 :)</td>', 'The only problem I have with this picture is that there is no sense of depth... It looks too me like I am looking straight down; however,  if you were to move the camara and point it more towards the sky (still keeping all sand in the pic) - maybe only 6-10 degreess more, this would be very pleasing... oringaly a 6, after reevaluation 8 :)', '2003-01-18 00:40:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(193797, 10821, 2700, '<td valign="top">the only problem here is that it seems blurry... I don''t know if that is the "smog" or your camera but if your camera has "infinate" focus (usually you will see a "mountain" symbol, that would defintaly help in this shot... If it wern''t for the blurrieness, easy 10....</td>', 'the only problem here is that it seems blurry... I don''t know if that is the "smog" or your camera but if your camera has "infinate" focus (usually you will see a "mountain" symbol, that would defintaly help in this shot... If it wern''t for the blurrieness, easy 10....', '2003-01-18 00:43:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(193798, 10885, 2700, '<td valign="top">almost "sureal" .. .nice effect , IR i guess ...</td>', 'almost "sureal" .. .nice effect , IR i guess ...', '2003-01-18 00:44:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(193799, 10788, 2700, '<td valign="top">in photoshop, there is this thing called levels... I Belive if you would  slide the "middle" slider more towards the left it would halp with more clarity/contrast in color/brightness on the rocks. I Dont know how to expain it in photography terms, but basicly you need to "allocate" less "bits" to the "black" range and more to the "white" range... <br/>check this out: //umsis.miami.edu/~jjuroch/10788edit.jpg <br/>still gave you a 10 though :)</td>', 'in photoshop, there is this thing called levels... I Belive if you would  slide the "middle" slider more towards the left it would halp with more clarity/contrast in color/brightness on the rocks. I Dont know how to expain it in photography terms, but basicly you need to "allocate" less "bits" to the "black" range and more to the "white" range... check this out: //umsis.miami.edu/~jjuroch/10788edit.jpg still gave you a 10 though :)', '2003-01-18 00:53:03.000000', NULL, 1),
