(195220, 10801, 6059, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hbunch7187:</b></div><hr/><i>Did you chose black and white cause the sky was white and blank?  I''m seeing white sky in a lot of shots this week.  must be the weather.  </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>no,in fact the sky was very cool, but the houses and the mountain were badly underlighted (or how it''s said)... so I just tried B&amp;W and it turned out much better...</td>', 'Originally posted by hbunch7187:Did you chose black and white cause the sky was white and blank?  I''m seeing white sky in a lot of shots this week.  must be the weather.    no,in fact the sky was very cool, but the houses and the mountain were badly underlighted (or how it''s said)... so I just tried B&W and it turned out much better...', '2003-01-20 03:40:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(195229, 10965, 5158, '<td valign="top">Thanx for all the wonderful and informative comments.<br/>Reading the comments is as exciting as looking at the vote.<br/> <br/>The outcome of my submission surprised my: I didn''t though it would do so well. 6.28 in this wonderful challenge is great.<br/> <br/>In my opinion my submission came short regarding the challenge-topic: the landscape was not the main object, it was more the weed. I also knew that some people might have problems realizing what they are looking at.<br/>Therefore I added this long title to strengthen the intention.<br/>Here is whole poem of Goethe for those who are interested:<br/> <br/>SAMENESS<br/>Over all hilltops<br/>is peace<br/>in all the treetops<br/>you feel<br/>barely a breeze;<br/>The birds in the forest have <br/>stopped their song<br/>Wait, before long<br/>you too will be still.<br/>(Translated by Brigitte Dubiel) <br/> <br/>I thought this poem fits well to the picture.<br/> <br/>I submitted the picture simply because I liked it very much for its simplicity.<br/>I had to crop it very tight, because in all directions there were other weeds disturbing the picture. I also sharpened it and strengthened the blue color.<br/>One big problem while taking the picture was that I could not judge it right on the spot: the sun shined so bright, that even with my sun-shade I could not see my LCD-screen well enough to determine sharpness and exposure correctly. It was also very cold, windy and I had to go into the deep snow with my knees to make the shot.<br/> <br/>Thanx again to all voters and commenter<br/> <br/>Jörg<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanx for all the wonderful and informative comments.Reading the comments is as exciting as looking at the vote. The outcome of my submission surprised my: I didn''t though it would do so well. 6.28 in this wonderful challenge is great. In my opinion my submission came short regarding the challenge-topic: the landscape was not the main object, it was more the weed. I also knew that some people might have problems realizing what they are looking at.Therefore I added this long title to strengthen the intention.Here is whole poem of Goethe for those who are interested: SAMENESSOver all hilltopsis peacein all the treetopsyou feelbarely a breeze;The birds in the forest have stopped their songWait, before longyou too will be still.(Translated by Brigitte Dubiel)  I thought this poem fits well to the picture. I submitted the picture simply because I liked it very much for its simplicity.I had to crop it very tight, because in all directions there were other weeds disturbing the picture. I also sharpened it and strengthened the blue color.One big problem while taking the picture was that I could not judge it right on the spot: the sun shined so bright, that even with my sun-shade I could not see my LCD-screen well enough to determine sharpness and exposure correctly. It was also very cold, windy and I had to go into the deep snow with my knees to make the shot. Thanx again to all voters and commenter Jörg ', '2003-01-20 04:41:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(195241, 10884, 3540, '<td valign="top">Critique Club by Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - A remarkable place you''ve chosen to shoot.  Very photo worthy.  The framing is great.  The angle this was taken from makes the shot.  Minimizing the sky has helped a lot.  Photos partly in the sun mostly in the shade are difficult to expose properly but it looks like you did a fine job of that.  The white sky is the only thing about this picture that I don''t like.  The slower shutter to show the motion of the water is the icing on the cake in this picture.  Great picture.<br/> <br/>Photography - Well I kinda covered this stuff in the last part.  ooops.  My bad.  In summary - you did a hell of a job<br/> <br/>Processing - Nothing is standing out.  The sky looks so white.  I don''t think you could''ve saturated some color into it without messing up something else.  Some things are better left untouched.<br/> <br/>Overall - An awesome scene well captured.  Nice job again Mag.  This is really well taken, meets the challenge well, and looks like a place where you could burn a card full in no time.</td>', 'Critique Club by Inspzil Composition - A remarkable place you''ve chosen to shoot.  Very photo worthy.  The framing is great.  The angle this was taken from makes the shot.  Minimizing the sky has helped a lot.  Photos partly in the sun mostly in the shade are difficult to expose properly but it looks like you did a fine job of that.  The white sky is the only thing about this picture that I don''t like.  The slower shutter to show the motion of the water is the icing on the cake in this picture.  Great picture. Photography - Well I kinda covered this stuff in the last part.  ooops.  My bad.  In summary - you did a hell of a job Processing - Nothing is standing out.  The sky looks so white.  I don''t think you could''ve saturated some color into it without messing up something else.  Some things are better left untouched. Overall - An awesome scene well captured.  Nice job again Mag.  This is really well taken, meets the challenge well, and looks like a place where you could burn a card full in no time.', '2003-01-20 05:28:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(195243, 10701, 5998, '<td valign="top">Thanks all of you!!</td>', 'Thanks all of you!!', '2003-01-20 05:29:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(195260, 10847, 749, '<td valign="top">For those of you who wondered what the thing on the left is, I went back to the same location a week later, and took <a href="//www.manic.nu/dpc/after-snow.jpg" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this photo</a> - it turns out to be a very oddly shaped waterfeature! :o) Final addition - it''s in fact the Canadian War Memorial... so now you know!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-03-16 12:05:10.</i></td>', 'For those of you who wondered what the thing on the left is, I went back to the same location a week later, and took this photo - it turns out to be a very oddly shaped waterfeature! :o) Final addition - it''s in fact the Canadian War Memorial... so now you know!', '2003-01-20 06:06:15.000000', '2003-03-16 12:05:10.000000', 0),
(195276, 10821, 1439, '<td valign="top">HI. thankz for the comments, No it''s not a pyramid and a powerplant ;) this is a mountain named "keilir" and the building is a restaurant named "perlan". "Perlan" joins and rests upon six hot water tanks each of which hold 4 million litres of hot water. (www.perlan.is) It is blurry because i used the digital zoom i only have 3x optical</td>', 'HI. thankz for the comments, No it''s not a pyramid and a powerplant ;) this is a mountain named "keilir" and the building is a restaurant named "perlan". "Perlan" joins and rests upon six hot water tanks each of which hold 4 million litres of hot water. (www.perlan.is) It is blurry because i used the digital zoom i only have 3x optical', '2003-01-20 06:43:55.000000', NULL, 0),
