(197248, 10811, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>Wow CC:</b> <br/>I''m excited to critique this interesting photo. I have few comments or suggestions to add here.<br/>Is this a landscape?.....well, no it''s not. I''m personally not a stickler for keeping exactly on the challenge. I do like people to be close to the ''challenge'' idea. Here I''m hoping that you live on a houseboat and that this is YOUR landscape. ;)&lt;wink,wink&gt;!<br/>Composition-Perfect, good perspective of the dock and boat. <br/> <br/>Background-Sunset....would be my guess, but it could be sunrise also.&lt;?&gt;<br/> <br/>Digital Processing-Wonderful DOF<br/> <br/>My Opinion-I hope you can tell by my earlier comment and this one that I like this shot very much and really wish there was a boat dock close by. I do love the light in this shot but would of liked the levels turned up just a bit. It was almost _too_ dark to take this shot. The goldish/pink reflection on the boats is wonderful along with the sky.<br/>Thanks for letting me voice my opinion of your photo. Hope you print and frame this one. It''s a keeper.<br/></td>', 'Wow CC: I''m excited to critique this interesting photo. I have few comments or suggestions to add here.Is this a landscape?.....well, no it''s not. I''m personally not a stickler for keeping exactly on the challenge. I do like people to be close to the ''challenge'' idea. Here I''m hoping that you live on a houseboat and that this is YOUR landscape. ;)<wink,wink>!Composition-Perfect, good perspective of the dock and boat.  Background-Sunset....would be my guess, but it could be sunrise also.<?> Digital Processing-Wonderful DOF My Opinion-I hope you can tell by my earlier comment and this one that I like this shot very much and really wish there was a boat dock close by. I do love the light in this shot but would of liked the levels turned up just a bit. It was almost _too_ dark to take this shot. The goldish/pink reflection on the boats is wonderful along with the sky.Thanks for letting me voice my opinion of your photo. Hope you print and frame this one. It''s a keeper.', '2003-01-21 19:20:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(197261, 10956, 2829, '<td valign="top">A visit from the critique club :)<br/> <br/>This is a cool photo. I like the colors but the sky is a bit washed out towards the middle. It''s bright. Perfectly exposed and has good focus. I like how you managed to fit the whole board-walkway into the shot. <br/> <br/>One thing that I think is missing here would be a good focal point for me to rest my eye on. It''s a pretty scene but it doesn''t draw me in enough.</td>', 'A visit from the critique club :) This is a cool photo. I like the colors but the sky is a bit washed out towards the middle. It''s bright. Perfectly exposed and has good focus. I like how you managed to fit the whole board-walkway into the shot.  One thing that I think is missing here would be a good focal point for me to rest my eye on. It''s a pretty scene but it doesn''t draw me in enough.', '2003-01-21 19:40:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(197277, 10866, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Flasher!<br/> <br/>I really like snow and ice winter scenes and I think that they can make terrific landscape shots as well.  In my humble opinion, this particular image is slightly weak for a landscape photo.  You have ''captured'' a landscape with your shot, but my mind is looking for something slightly more dramatic with higher impact.  Maybe a wider-scale scene with some more ''land'' showing here would create that impact.  <br/> <br/>The lighting here creates some nice shadow for your shot as well.  The shadow areas contain a bit of a ''blue'' cast... possibly caused by a polarizing filter?  Not completely sure about that but... when this happens, you can often correct it by desaturating the blue/cyan channels in photoshop :)  I think that could improve this image just a bit as well.<br/> <br/>Keep up the great work :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Flasher! I really like snow and ice winter scenes and I think that they can make terrific landscape shots as well.  In my humble opinion, this particular image is slightly weak for a landscape photo.  You have ''captured'' a landscape with your shot, but my mind is looking for something slightly more dramatic with higher impact.  Maybe a wider-scale scene with some more ''land'' showing here would create that impact.   The lighting here creates some nice shadow for your shot as well.  The shadow areas contain a bit of a ''blue'' cast... possibly caused by a polarizing filter?  Not completely sure about that but... when this happens, you can often correct it by desaturating the blue/cyan channels in photoshop :)  I think that could improve this image just a bit as well. Keep up the great work :) John Setzler', '2003-01-21 19:56:55.000000', NULL, 0),
